# J51 — Emptiness probe via the paused-prompt ':' route
# Recovers J42's blocked question: does the explicit worklist verb land on
# honest empty guidance (no fabricated rows), given that Setup pauses the
# command prompt and requires ':' to type a command?
name: Empty worklist and scene via colon route
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
launch: --target @TARGET
wait-for: 30 KUZUSHI
wait: 2
keys: :
type: worklist
keys: Enter
wait: 3
snap: worklist-empty
ask: Did the worklist verb land on ONE empty-guidance panel (no risk worklist + context:build/worklist:rank CTAs), zero fabricated rows — or did the keystrokes get swallowed again?
keys: Escape
keys: q
submit: scene
wait: 2
snap: scene-empty
ask: On a target with no artifacts, does the scene gallery page show one guidance line per empty page (empty_hint), never dummy content?
keys: Tab
wait: 1
snap: scene-tab-2
keys: Tab
wait: 1
snap: scene-tab-3
ask: Do empty pages stay out of the Tab rail (gate-on-non-empty) or does Tab stop on blank pages?
